  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' (ID `d3d7af60-4c81-11e8-b3d7-01146121b73d`) has 33 fields. They include `Carrier`, `Cancelled`, `Origin`, `Dest`, `AvgTicketPrice` and `FlightDelay`. Its time field is `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** 'S4-605c3928 Flights' (ID `75c2edb0-312c-4db4-b0f0-d70b7fe57d84`) has exactly two panels. One is a line chart of flights over time (count by `timestamp`). The other is a bar chart of the top 10 carriers by flight count.\n3. **Rule:** 'S4-605c3928 Cancelled flights' (ID `6429559a-efd3-4066-81d0-509e7a31daae`) is an index-threshold rule. It runs every minute and counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_flights` where `Cancelled:true`. It fires when the count over 5 minutes is above 10. It was created enabled, so I didn't need to enable it afterwards. It has no actions, so it won't notify anyone when it fires.\n4. **Edit and read-back:** The carrier panel's title is now 'Flights by carrier', and the other panel is unchanged. Reading the rule back shows `enabled: true`, and its last run had status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
